## Hazards emitted (from the L06 trade-off matrix)

| ID | Severity | Axis | Hazard |
|----|----------|------|--------|
| HZ-01 | **HIGH** | risk | **Durable scar poisoning.** Persistence converts a self-limiting defect (a bad scar dies at process exit) into a permanent cross-run poison vector injected into every matching future goal. |
| HZ-02 | **HIGH** | accuracy/maintainability | **Contract drift.** `DurableScarStore` diverging from the in-memory `ScarStore` (match semantics, `INJECTION_STAGES` gating, ordering, `get_precedent`) breaks L18 injection assumptions — or the change breaks the existing store/tests. |
| HZ-03 | **HIGH** | accuracy | **Scar-ID instability across reopen.** A counter reset mints duplicate `scar-NNNN` ids, making `get_precedent` ambiguous and shadowing older lessons. |
| HZ-04 | MEDIUM | risk/latency | **SQLite contention/corruption** of `state_dir/scars.db` under `ConcurrentScheduler` parallel runs (`SQLITE_BUSY`, partial writes). |
| HZ-05 | MEDIUM | latency/memory | **I/O overhead**: full row load on construction + write-through on every `propose_scar` vs the zero-cost in-memory dict. |
| HZ-06 | LOW | maintainability | **No schema migration path** for `scars.db` when the scar record shape evolves. |
| HZ-07 | LOW | memory/latency | **Unbounded scar growth** inflates `match_scars` cost and `_scar_refs` injection payloads. |
| HZ-08 | MEDIUM | risk (environment) | **Homogeneous-audit window**: implementation/seal run GLM-5.3-only until ~2026-08-22. |

## Safeguards bound to hazards

| ID | Hazard | Mechanism | Safeguard |
|----|--------|-----------|-----------|
| SG-01 | HZ-01 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **T3 quarantine before any durable write.** `propose_scar` raises `ScarQuarantined` for signatures with `< MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS` *before* write-through; over-broad scars can never reach `scars.db`. Proven by the durability test's quarantine case. |
| SG-02 | HZ-01 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **Subset-containment match frozen.** `scar.signature <= goal_tags` via `parse_signature`; a durable scar injects only into goals meeting ALL its conditions. Shared logic reused (not reimplemented) so the two stores cannot drift. |
| SG-03 | HZ-01 | KILL_SWITCH | **Single-file memory reset.** `scars.db` is a plain SQLite file colocated with `ledger.db`; deleting it restores the zero-scar baseline, and reverting the `SoftLoop(scar_store=...)` wiring restores today's in-memory behavior. Blast radius never touches ledger/CAS. |
| SG-04 | HZ-02 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **Contract-parity freeze.** Exact `ScarStore` surface (`propose_scar`, `match_scars`, `get_precedent`, `injected_scars` gated by `INJECTION_STAGES`); in-memory store and its tests untouched and green. Gate: `uv run pytest -q tests/runtime/test_scar_durability.py tests/runtime/test_scars.py tests/runtime/test_evolution.py`. |
| SG-05 | HZ-03 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **ID stability across reopen.** Counter derived at construction from max existing `scar-NNNN` row id; ids immutable once written. Durability test asserts same id from a fresh instance. |
| SG-06 | HZ-04 | FALLBACK | **Proven-concurrency pattern + fail-loud bootstrap.** SQLite file locking arbitrates cross-process access; in-process L3 authoring already single-committer (`evolution_lock`, IP-0005). If `scars.db` cannot be opened, `build_scheduler` fails loud (fail-loud invoker policy) rather than silently masquerading as durable. |

